# Agent instructions for <PROJECT NAME>

This file is read by agent tools that look for `AGENTS.md` (Codex, Cursor, and others).
It intentionally mirrors `CLAUDE.md` — keep the two in sync, or make one a pointer to
the other, but never let them disagree. Contradictory instruction files are worse than
one file, because whichever tool reads the stale one behaves confidently wrong.

See `CLAUDE.md` in this directory for the full project instructions.

## The short version

- <one sentence: what this project is>
- Build: `<command>` · Test: `<command>` · Lint: `<command>`
- Never post, release, void, or reverse a document without explicit human approval.
